fixup! Bug 2061218 - Save calendar event edits in new calendar edit dialog. r=#thunderbird-front-end-reviewers

Failure causes:
Two test defects remain in current source. test_keyboardSaveClearsStateAndUpdatesCalendar skips the visible More button between Calendar and Close. Enter therefore activates Close instead of Save, causing the focus, storage, cleanup, and Redo failures in jobs 601216784, 601216651, 601216831, 601216703, and 601216761. test_invalidActiveFieldsBlockSave synthesizes a pointer event over disabled Save. Hit testing reaches the footer and triggers the accessibility failure in job 601216651. The supplied assessment covers 100 jobs with no unknown classifications; its other 95 classifications remain unchanged.

Related Try b9c25e72-201d-4b57-89f9-c23089f51094:
Job 601561258 exposes a real lifecycle error. storeObserver subscribes during construction. Replacing a connected calendar dialog dispatches a store update before the replacement's connectedCallback creates its body. #renderSave then calls setAttribute on null. The current source still contained this access. The supplied assessment covers 45 jobs; its other 44 unrelated classifications remain unchanged. Existing PointerEvent crashes and baseline accessibility failures are not resolved by this repair.

Changes:
Changed only mail/components/calendar/test/browser/browser_calendarEventEditSave.js: 31 added lines and four removed lines. The keyboard test now checks More visibility and Calendar → More → Close → Save, reverse navigation, and forward navigation again before Enter. It retains accessibility, storage, focus restoration, route cleanup, Undo, and Redo assertions. The invalid-field test uses button.click() for disabled Save and explains why pointer events reach the footer. It retains direct Save rejection, zero transactions, draft retention, unchanged storage, retry, and pointer coverage for enabled Save. The shared edit() helper now supplies the message "The edited event dialog should open." The resulting file exactly matches prior fixups 732f474f974fe002762aa87d5bb172ef39e416bc and da851aba75b578592b65b80435553181d5e4a14c. These repairs were still needed because the file was unchanged across all sourceUpdates revisions and current HEAD. The indexed description-row, Account Hub, and password-manager repairs address separate code; none was duplicated. The actual diff follows all three prepared evidence decisions, with no departures.

Related Try b9c25e72-201d-4b57-89f9-c23089f51094:
mail/components/calendar/content/calendar-event-create-edit-dialog.mjs now queries the body and returns before rendering when the body is absent. A comment explains the subscription timing. Once content exists, Save rendering retains its busy state, dismissal lock, button state, calendar control, focus handling, and status announcements. mail/components/calendar/test/browser/browser_calendarEventEditSave.js adds test_storeUpdatesBeforeConnection. It constructs a detached replacement, triggers a real store update through another dialog, replaces that dialog, and checks readiness, stored draft content, Save availability, aria-busy, and native dismissal. Cleanup removes dialogs and subscriptions. All nine new assertions have expected-behavior messages containing should. The diff follows the collected evidence; the early return follows the direct user instruction instead of copying the accepted example's nested guard. No related repairs, source updates, or prior fixup were supplied.

Validation:
Prior checks for the separate repairs:
Passed node --check and git diff --check. Passed ESLint 9.39.1 with --no-cache and Prettier 3.8.5 --check. Direct ESLint used the current comm configuration, copies of the current in-tree Mozilla and SDL plugins, and installed dependencies. Inspected the resolved browser-test globals and preference restrictions. A syntax-tree audit checked all 43 assertions in the repaired tasks and shared opener: every message is non-empty, states the expected behavior, and contains should. A separate comparison found that all existing assertion calls remain unchanged except the intended opener message; the file has 127 assertions versus 123 before repair. Attempted the native Mochitest harness with AUTOCLOBBER=1, MOZ_HEADLESS=1, --flavor browser, --subsuite thunderbird, --headless, and browser_calendarEventEditSave.js. The copied harness, current Calendar tests, profiles, temporary files, and logs stayed inside comm/obj-repair-validation. After resolving declared Python dependencies, startup stopped during ssltunnel process cleanup with PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: 'ps'. Final status contains only the intended test modification. HEAD and its parent remain unchanged, and nothing is staged.

Passed: a source-level experiment using the real Redux store, storeObserver, and extracted production rendering methods. The original renderer threw TypeError before connection; the repaired renderer passed detached, idle, pending, failure, focus, and success checks with a stub DOM. An AST check confirmed all nine new browser assertion messages. Direct ESLint passed for both changed files using this checkout's configuration and Mozilla rules, with existing dependencies resolved through a temporary loader. Prettier --check, node --check for both files, and git diff --check passed. The complete two-file repair passed git apply --check against ancestor 848790d0f4c1fd67b2ecc527eee8bbec8c13947b with one line of context. Final status contains only the two intended source changes; HEAD remains unchanged.

The console combined the exact repair deltas. Fresh Try runs must validate the cumulative source.

Validation limits:
No native browser test passed. Normal and accessibility runtime validation remain incomplete because the harness stopped before launching tests. The available build is marked incomplete and reports SourceStamp=unknown, so it cannot establish matching-source success. No visible browser was used. The mach commlint wrapper was not repeated after its documented setup-write failures; direct lint success does not establish every wrapper check. The independent evidence assessment remains incomplete. No accepted local example covers the complete Save Tab sequence or disabled Save activation; these are scoped repairs supported by current source and failure logs, not shared rules. The audit confirmed 43 untouched message-less assertions elsewhere in the file; they remain outside this repair. Ignored validation files are excluded. No commits, staging, Git ref changes, shared-rule changes, or writes outside this comm checkout were performed.

The official headless browser harness was attempted with AUTOCLOBBER=1 for browser_calendarEventEditSave.js. It stopped before launching Thunderbird because macOS denied psutil's process scan: PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted (originated from sysctl() malloc 1/3). Native execution, browser regression failure sensitivity, and accessibility validation remain incomplete. The stub-DOM experiment is not browser validation. ../mach commlint also stopped before checking code because it could not create obj-try-monitor/.mozbuild/logs/commlint outside comm; direct ESLint and Prettier completed separately. No build or full Try ran. The evidence assessment remains incomplete and is not claimed as verification. Temporary diagnostic files were removed. No files were staged or committed, and no Git refs or shared rules were changed.

An earlier Try does not validate this new cumulative fixup.

